Role inference for symbol refs:
- scan source text (per module) for regex of the symbol name:
  - write if `NAME.write_text|NAME.write_bytes|json.dump(... NAME ...)|yaml.safe_dump(... NAME)|open(NAME, 'w')`
  - exec if `str(NAME)` inside subprocess args or `[sys.executable, str(NAME)`.
  - read if `NAME.read_text|json.loads(NAME.read_text())|yaml.safe_load(...NAME...)|json.load(NAME)|open(NAME)` or NAME appears as an argument to a subprocess tool (exec implies read).
  Determine mode: if any write-context and no read/exec → write; else read; if `str(NAME)` near subprocess → exec.
Actually simplest robust approach per symbol: use AST to find all Name loads and check the enclosing call/attribute:
- If name appears as `NAME.write_text(...)` or as arg in `json.dump(x, NAME.open('w'))` → write.
- If name appears as `str(NAME)` within a `subprocess.run([...])` call → exec.
- If name appears in any other expression → read (conservative).
